    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 274 tests, 0 failures, including the cp12 acceptance tests and all prior checkpoints.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task (checkpoint cp12) is implemented. When creating an owner (`POST /api/owners`), the city is now title-cased, unless an owner already exists in that same city \u2014 in which case the existing owner's exact spelling is reused.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`CityNormalizer.java`** (new) \u2014 a utility with `titleCase(...)` that upper-cases the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest (e.g. `\"riverdale5\"` \u2192 `\"Riverdale5\"`), preserving existing whitespace and returning `null` for `null`.\n\n2. **`NormalizeCity.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor function step that:\n   - looks up existing owners and, if one has a city matching case-insensitively, reuses that exact spelling;\n   - otherwise stores the title-cased city.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `normalizeCity` step between `build` and `rejectDuplicate` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`), so it runs before `assignCustomerCode`, keeping the per-city customer code derived from the canonical city spelling.\n\nThis follows the repo's existing conventions (a package-private normalizer utility like `TelephoneNormalizer`/`DuplicateMatching`, single-public-method function classes reading state via `@Val Owner`).",
